    "policy": "Separate stock and inner-ink fit on frozen PLC poses; shared stock, per-source ink.\nFit the lower quartile of near-black source residuals to reduce bright edge/texture contamination.\nA fixed 96-byte transition preserves all brighter pigment; thin lines cannot identify its shape reliably.\nSource-guided inner samples omit transparent art, lettering and boundary AA.\nThin keylines cannot survive a full-pixel erosion, so report pose sensitivity.\n",
